    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0306" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/5–2148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in the United Kingdom
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-22T14:00:00-04:00">May 22, 1948—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1877. For Douglas from Lovett. Proceed along lines indicated urtel 2214,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d176-f1"/>
                    endeavoring to persuade French and checking British position re your suggestion
                    concurred in by Clay, Murphy and Reber. Do not commit us as we need time to get top level
                    clearance here.</p>
                <p>Assume Clay has taken into account that
                    announcement concerning provisional govt may give Soviets excuse to intensify
                    pressure in Berlin, also that US and British Delegations feel danger of delay in
                    Germany is greater than risks involved in Soviet reaction.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d176-f2"/> [Lovett.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d176-f1" n="1" xml:id="d176-f1-content">
                <p>May 21, <ref target="#pg266">p. 266</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d176-f2" n="2" xml:id="d176-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 2233, May 24, from London, not printed, Ambassador Douglas confirmed that the assumptions stated
                    here were correct (740.00119 Council/5–2448).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
